{
    "background_story": "Muffy was a vintage Volkswagen Beetle with a personality as bright as her cherry-red paint job. She had been restored to her former glory by her owner, a mechanic with a passion for classic cars. One of Muffy's most distinctive features was her unique taillight design, which had been hand-crafted by her owner to resemble a pair of gleaming red eyes. As Muffy cruised down the highway, her taillights would light up the night, warning other drivers of her approach. But Muffy's taillights were more than just a safety feature - they had become a trademark of sorts, earning her a reputation as the coolest ride in town. Wherever Muffy went, her taillights would announce her arrival, and people would smile as they caught a glimpse of her retro charm.",
